## Lore

The Sovietski police are a branch of the Red Army assigned to civil defense
and law enforcement in New Moscow and the cities, towns and villages around
it. They handle the day to day business of each community: crime, civil
unrest, smugglers, spies, the local Black Market and terrorists.

The line between police and army is thin. Both answer to the same government,
both can search homes and make arrests, and they wear much the same armor and
carry the same weapons, told apart mostly by color: police red and grey with a
red star. The police are seen as the junior service, with less field
experience, and they call in the Army when a threat is too large or too
supernatural to contain.

Most officers are partial cyborgs or Light Machines, nearly always with a
human-looking face. Detectives work in plain clothes.

## GM Notes

The block prints no Money line and no salary; starting money is the GM''s call.

Vehicle: an M.D.C. motorcycle, 75 M.D.C. main body and 8 per wheel. On
assignment: jet pack and other vehicles, additional weapons, explosives and
equipment, plus access to police facilities, computers and back-up.
Availability depends on the local commander, supply, location and combat
conditions.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: an energy pistol and an energy rifle
of choice (Triax weapons included; the G-21P and S-20-20 pistols are the most
popular). Detectives also get a suit, long coat, scarf, gloves and boots. A
Light Machine or partial ''Borg also gets the ammunition, equipment and body
armor suited to the cyborg body and its weapon systems, with regular
maintenance and repairs.

Typical bionics: 30% are 55% conversion partial cyborgs, 25% are 70-80%
conversion partial ''Borgs, 25% are full conversion Light Machines, and 20% are
completely human with 1D4 implants. All but 2% of cyborg police keep a
human-looking face and head.

Common cyborg police features: full 20/20 enhanced color vision; targeting
sight (+1 to strike) and light filters; telescopic eye with passive
nightvision (5000 ft); multi-system eye socket; universal headjack/ear implant
with augmentation; amplified audio; built-in language translator; built-in
radio transmitter and receiver (5 miles); two cyberlink vehicle interfaces
(hand and head); Gromeko Friend or Foe Identification Computer; bionic lung
with gas filter and oxygen storage cell; bionic running speed of 120 mph;
leaping 12 feet high or 18 feet long, half again as far with a running start.

Combat/police systems: one forearm weapon on each arm (typically laser or
ion), a concealed Vibro-Blade and a wrist climb cord and grapple, plus 1D4+2
optional systems of choice from: chemical spray, palm laser torch, camera
finger, laser finger (1D4 M.D., 300 ft), tool hand, built-in loudspeaker,
molecular analyzer, cyber-shield, cyber-disguise (either type). Police avoid
anything disfiguring, especially to the face.

Secondary skills start at level 2 (two each at levels 2, 4, 8 and 13). The
save vs Horror Factor rises by +1 at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12.
